  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_037: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) achieves 0.7062 accuracy. The only untested dimension within this best-performing combination is the aggregation method. Prior evidence (pca_n2000: avgpool 0.591 vs transformer 0.519) suggests avgpool may be preferred, but that was with a linear encoder; scvi_n200 produces richer, non-linear embeddings where a transformer could better capture inter-profile interactions. Config_039 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) is a clean single-variable ablation of the current best, directly testing whether transformer aggregation can push performance above 0.7062 or confirm avgpool as optimal. This is the highest-value next step: it either yields a new best or definitively closes the aggregation question for the top-performing pipeline, allowing the remaining budget to focus on other axes (e.g., scgpt multimodal or singleprofile variants)."
